  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> to be continuous at <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> we must have<br /><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mroot><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mroot><mo>-</mo><mroot><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mroot></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></m